WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.453
Free text is a contract nobody signed.

2
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:10.499
This week you’ll build the core of the studio project: reading a meeting transcript and producing action items your code can act on.

3
00:00:10.779 --> 00:00:17.797
The moment a model’s output feeds another program (a tracker, a database, a dashboard), its job changes.

4
00:00:18.077 --> 00:00:23.837
A person reading “Priya will send finance the budget, probably by the 20th” understands it.

5
00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:29.877
A program needs to know which field is the owner, which is the date, and what format the date is in.

6
00:00:30.157 --> 00:00:36.365
Ask a model for “the action items as JSON” in plain prose and you’ll see a familiar set of failures.

7
00:00:36.645 --> 00:00:43.088
Sometimes there’s a friendly sentence before the JSON, or the JSON arrives wrapped in a Markdown code fence.

8
00:00:43.368 --> 00:00:46.675
A key is called owner on one run and assignee on the next.

9
00:00:46.955 --> 00:00:48.960
A date arrives as “next Friday.

10
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.715
” A field your code needs is simply missing.

11
00:00:51.995 --> 00:01:06.096
Anthropic’s structured outputs documentation lists the same categories: invalid JSON syntax, missing required fields, inconsistent data types, and schema violations that force you to write error handling and retries.

12
00:01:06.376 --> 00:01:08.808
None of this means the model is bad at the task.

13
00:01:09.088 --> 00:01:12.821
It means nothing told it, or checked, what shape the answer must have.

14
00:01:13.101 --> 00:01:19.907
Every one of these failures is about shape, and shape is something you can specify exactly and verify mechanically.

15
00:01:20.187 --> 00:01:21.701
That’s the job of a schema.

16
00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:26.717
Lesson 8 shows how to make the API enforce a schema during generation.

17
00:01:26.997 --> 00:01:37.024
This lesson covers the schema itself and the validation you run no matter which API you use, because validation is your check on any output, from any provider.
